+# Histogram continuity, 2026-10-10
+
+Requirements RR06/V03/V05/Q01; preserve R01, TD06/TD08, pinned track/car comparison contracts, normal results first, five laps, best-only scoring and public/artificial isolation. The owner reports the same histogram briefly appearing, disappearing and reappearing in Free Race.
+
+The metadata preview already had a warmed comparison packet. When the compiled target had a local PB, its separate candidate/marker read could remain pending after the preview was replaced with an empty pinned snapshot. Separately, late standings or PB changes rebuilt the entire detail row, destroying and recreating the chart controls despite unchanged histogram data. The regression fixture reproduced both: **seven checks, four failures** before the correction. [Baseline log](evidence/histogram-continuity-2026-10-10/continuity-before.log).
+
+`game/ui/track_browser.gd` now promotes a valid warmed packet into the pinned record snapshot before the compiled view is drawn, applying the actual local/verified marker values. It preserves the existing request decision, including local-PB overlays, without adding background polling. The populated comparison column survives metadata promotion and unrelated detail updates for the same immutable version, vehicle and account/service scope. Actual count or marker changes update the same controls and request a redraw. Different tracks, cars or scopes cannot retain that column. Confirmed empty metrics rebuild their proper empty layout; failed reads without valid cached data still show the existing unavailable state. No new player-facing text was added.
+
+Changed files: `game/ui/track_browser.gd`; new `game/tests/test_histogram_continuity.gd` and its generated UID; this report; `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md`; `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md`. No canonical simulation, backend API, schema or rules contract changed. [Task-only Git checkpoint](evidence/histogram-continuity-2026-10-10/scoped-change.patch) preserves unrelated workspace work.
+
+Actual commands use `powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1`, pinned Godot **4.7.2 stable ed1daf0bf**, isolated `APPDATA=build/histogram-continuity-*-user`, and `-CommandTimeoutSeconds 90`:
+
+- `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_histogram_continuity.gd -Graphical`: **15 checks, zero failures**. Both histograms remain visible with the same controls and exact counts across **all 36 sampled geometry-handoff frames**, while the local-PB request is deliberately held. Late standings preserve the controls; genuinely changed server counts update in place; a different car cannot borrow the old charts, and its actual empty response remains explicit. [Log](evidence/histogram-continuity-2026-10-10/continuity-final.log), [per-frame observations](evidence/histogram-continuity-2026-10-10/frames.json).
+- `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_instant_comparisons.gd`: **25 checks, zero failures**, including scoped caching, foreground priority and genuine empty fields. [Log](evidence/histogram-continuity-2026-10-10/instant-final.log).
+- `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_carousel_histograms.gd`: **20 checks, zero failures**, including preview-before-geometry, rapid far-track selections and bounded warming. [Log](evidence/histogram-continuity-2026-10-10/carousel-final.log).
+- `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_unified_histograms.gd`, with `BMT_RESULTS_EVIDENCE=docs/evidence/histogram-continuity-2026-10-10/unified`: **127 checks, zero failures**. [Log](evidence/histogram-continuity-2026-10-10/unified-final.log).
+- `TestApp`: **99 checks, zero failures**. [Log](evidence/histogram-continuity-2026-10-10/app-final.log).
+- Scoped `git diff --check` and reverse Git checkpoint validation: pass.
+
+An intermediate retention condition kept old controls when the fixture explicitly cleared all valid comparison data and returned a failure. The unchanged unified suite caught this (**127 checks, one failure**); the guard now distinguishes a pending handoff from a completed failure without usable data. Its final rerun passes. No assertion was removed or weakened.
+
+Inspected native captures: [metadata preview](evidence/histogram-continuity-2026-10-10/preview-ready.png), [compiled track with the local-PB read still pending](evidence/histogram-continuity-2026-10-10/compiled-read-pending.png), [late standings ready](evidence/histogram-continuity-2026-10-10/standings-ready.png). The test uses a retained actual Slippery comparison packet with synthetic local track names/PB values and isolated mock responses. Its count-change case is an explicit test packet, not a submitted race or live server update. No server/player data was written.
+
+The original scenic preview and metadata-only race gate remain; actual compiled tracks retain race availability while optional data loads. Legitimate new counts, markers or timing bounds may still change the chart's appearance. These checks prove the reproduced handoff and refresh paths, not every device or network timing. No phone attachment check or physical-device test was performed. No Android export/install, full Validate, backend deployment or production action was performed. Remaining acceptance: restart the updated client and review actual populated Free Race transitions on the owner's device.
